Lets the two inference APIs of the Citadel gateway-upgrade module log token counts without logging a prompt or an answer.

The module passes the LLM log settings of its parameters straight to the API-level Azure Monitor diagnostic. The service
refuses the value "none" for the messages of a request or a response ("Invalid field
'largeLanguageModel.requests.messages' specified"): to log no messages, the request and the response settings have to be left
out. The patch leaves them out when the parameter says "none", and passes them on as before for any other value.

It applies to bicep/infra/modules/apim/inference-api.bicep of the kit at the commit that the workflows check out
(Azure-Samples/ai-hub-gateway-solution-accelerator, citadel-v1); the checks apply it for real. The kit's unified-ai-api.bicep has
the same two lines; that API is not deployed here, so it is not patched.

diff --git a/bicep/infra/modules/apim/inference-api.bicep b/bicep/infra/modules/apim/inference-api.bicep
--- a/bicep/infra/modules/apim/inference-api.bicep
+++ b/bicep/infra/modules/apim/inference-api.bicep
@@ -195,11 +195,11 @@ resource apiDiagnostics 'Microsoft.ApiManagement/service/apis/diagnostics@2024-0
     }
     largeLanguageModel: {
       logs: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.logs
-      requests: {
+      requests: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.requests.messages == 'none' ? null : {
         messages: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.requests.messages
         maxSizeInBytes: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.requests.maxSizeInBytes
       }
-      responses: {
+      responses: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.responses.messages == 'none' ? null : {
         messages: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.responses.messages
         maxSizeInBytes: azureMonitorLogSettings.largeLanguageModel.responses.maxSizeInBytes
       }
